# cst/GAPS: the constructs NetlistParse.rs d565fd3's Spectre CST cannot parse (Incomplete/Error nodes on
# manual-valid input, VAMOS_SPECTRE_DESIGN.md §11.1, §13 E88) and the node groups it truncates, each with
# the vamos-authored lang/ fixture that covers it.  tests/vamos/test_spectre_cst_oracle.py asserts vamos's
# reading of the fixture (the statement kinds listed here, in order) and skips the CST comparison for the
# fixture's Incomplete/Error statements; a fixture not listed here must tile and compare clean.  Every
# line is used by the oracle (an unused line fails the suite).
#
# construct | lang fixture (relative to fixtures/spectre) | vamos's statement kinds, in order | [M cite]
model group { k: ... } | lang/model_group.scs | model | [M UG p.108]
statistics block | lang/statistics.scs | parameters statistics | [M ref19 pp.175-179]
sweep { ... } body | lang/sweep_block.scs | parameters analysis | [M ref19 p.406]
sweep { ... } body (vector elements) | lang/vector_elements.scs | parameters analysis analysis | [M ref19 pp.406, 477]
montecarlo { ... } body with export | lang/montecarlo_block.scs | analysis | [M ref19 p.175]
bare instance node list (r1 a b resistor) | lang/bare_nodes.scs | instance instance instance | [M UG p.60]
a title line (line 1 is never a statement) | lang/title_line.scs | instance | [M UG p.29]
a line-1 * comment | lang/star_comment.scs | instance instance | [M UG p.59]
the escaped name r\2 | lang/escaped_name.scs | instance model instance | [M UG pp.60-62]
the brace-less if | lang/braceless_if.scs | parameters if if | [M UG p.109]
library / section / endsection / endlibrary | lang/library.scs | library | [M UG pp.75-76]
protect / unprotect, prot / unprot in any case | lang/prot.scs | protect instance unprotect protect instance unprotect | [M ref19 p.497]
save modifiers (depth= sigtype= devtype= exclude= time_window= ports= filter=) | lang/save_modifiers.scs | save save save save | [M ref19 p.517]
a one-line real function | lang/oneline_function.scs | function parameters | [M UG p.92]
node groups (1 2)(3 4), which the CST truncates after the first group | lang/node_groups.scs | instance instance | [M UG p.30; E93]
